          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Theresa787"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was absolutely delicious. Thank you for sharing. I omitted the fresh basil (didn't have any at the time). I cooked the salmon fillets in aluminum foil packets at 425 degrees for 12 minutes (my husband doesn't like the smell of fish cooking). The salmon was tender and flavorful. We'll definitely be making this again.",
            "datePublished": "2011-10-12T16:57:24.630Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RedCook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am so glad that I found this recipe! It tasted great! I didn’t make any changes to the main ingredients, but had to leave out the basil garnish since I didn’t have it on hand. I was only able to marinate the salmon in the fridge for an hour instead of 2 so I can only imagine how much tastier it would be! Also, I ended up cooking it in parchment as that’s how I like to cook my fish. This recipe is definitely going into the regular rotation.",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-15T15:06:22.167Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mencancook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Followed the recipe exactly with the result being one of the best tasting salmon dishes I have ever had. I did sprinkle some salt on each filet just prior to grilling. I made double the marinade and used it for broccoli that I also grilled. That was paired with with dill rice for a very memorable meal. Easy and delicious, will definitely go into the rotation.",
            "datePublished": "2019-07-04T17:10:36.563Z"
          },
          {
